// The logs feature's PUBLIC API — re-exports only.
//
// The screen itself is the `logspage` RECORD, mounted by `LogsGraphHost` — which is what
// `lazyWorkspaces` resolves the `LogsWorkspace` symbol to, in both App.tsx and DetachedWindow.
//
// This feature WAS `features/security`. The Security workspace held four tabs; three were deleted
// (retire-agentprofile-and-strip-security-to-activity) and Activity — the only one with a real feed
// behind it — became the first tab of the unified Logs screen (epic-a-unified-logs-workspace). The
// remaining tabs (Sessions, Waiting, Skills, Hooks, Cost, Streams) read the `bsc logs` engine (#1607).
//
// WHAT DID NOT COME HERE, and why. `agentProfiles`, `profileEnforcement` and `consoleModel` moved to
// `shared/lib/security` instead: they are read by the console shell, the planner, the tunnel projector
// AND the store, so a feature was never their owner — the shell was reaching into a feature's internals
// to get them, which is exactly what #1545 forbids. Logs imports them from `shared/`, like anyone else.
//
// The `AgentProfile` model is still ENFORCED at launch via `resolveProfileSettings` →
// `ensure_session_settings`, and allowlists still resolve additively (guaranteed ∪ profile ∪ project ∪
// repo). Retiring the model needs a coordinated mobile-studio-code change — the tunnel ships it against
// a byte-exact fixture — and is tracked as `retire-the-agentprofile-model-behind-the-tunnel-contract`.

// The graph-hosted workspace (#3646) — App.tsx/DetachedWindow render this via the lazy LogsWorkspace.
export { LogsGraphHost } from "@/features/logs/LogsGraphHost";

// #1545: public API for cross-feature consumers. The audit feed's derivation is shared with the tunnel
// projector (#3754), which derives its consoles + display rows the SAME way this screen does — one
// source of truth for the pane→console join and the allow/ask/block verdict.
export { parseAuditLog, type AuditRecord } from "@/features/logs/lib/auditLog";
export { buildAuditRows, type AuditDisplayRow } from "@/features/logs/lib/auditRows";
